    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Our Gas Safe Plumber Checks at Your St Helens Property</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We cover the boiler, gas cooker and hob. Each one is inspected individually and recorded on the CP12. Open-flue appliances receive the extra checks they need.</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Gas supply pressure and flow rate</strong><p>Gas pressure tested at the meter and at each appliance. Low pressure or restricted flow can cause appliances to operate unsafely.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Gas leak check</strong><p>All pipework and appliance connections tested for gas leaks. Any leak classified under the Gas Industry Unsafe Situations Procedure and addressed before we leave.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Flue integrity and combustion spillage</strong><p>All flues tested for integrity and safe discharge. Open-flue appliances receive a combustion spillage test to confirm combustion products are not entering the room. This is legally required for open-flue appliances.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Ventilation adequacy</strong><p>Each appliance we cover is checked for adequate ventilation. Particularly important in older WA10 terraces where ventilation is often inadequate or blocked.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Safety device operation</strong><p>All appliance safety devices tested individually. Each must demonstrate correct operation before the appliance can pass the inspection.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Signs of incomplete combustion</strong><p>Checked for staining, sooting or carbon deposits. Particularly important for open-flue appliances, where CO risk is higher than for sealed flue boilers.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Boiler, gas cooker and hob</strong><p>Each one inspected individually and recorded separately on the CP12. We do not inspect gas fires or back boilers. Tell us about them when you book and we will explain your options.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>CP12 certificate issued and emailed same day</strong><p>Digital CP12 emailed the same day. Includes the engineer's Gas Safe registration number, inspection date and result for every appliance checked.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


